│ patch_description        │ Replace the random Gaussian cloud with a symmetric 14-point cube–octahedron compound. The │
│                          │ eight cube vertices and six coordinate-axis vertices provide a much more uniform          │
│                          │ diameter-bounded packing than random points.                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The axis radius is chosen as `sqrt(3)`, equal to the cube circumradius. This keeps the    │
│                          │ maximum distance at the cube diameter while maximizing the limiting cube-to-axis distance │
│                          │ within this symmetric family. The resulting configuration has a deterministic squared     │
│                          │ minimum/maximum ratio of approximately `(6 - 2*sqrt(3)) / 12 = 0.2113`, vastly improving  │
│                          │ on an unconstrained random sample, while returning exactly a finite `(14, 3)` NumPy       │
│                          │ array.                                                                                    │
