│ patch_name               │ diameter_aware_continuation                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ This replaces the unstructured Gaussian sample with a deterministic, diameter-aware       │
│                          │ packing optimizer. The construction begins from several geometrically diverse seeds,      │
│                          │ including Fibonacci-sphere layouts, staggered latitude-ring layouts, and reproducible     │
│                          │ randomized spherical layouts.                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The novel optimization uses a continuation objective with two coupled smooth terms: a     │
│                          │ soft minimum of squared pair distances and a soft maximum of squared pair distances. It   │
│                          │ therefore improves the actual evaluator target directly, rather than only spreading       │
│                          │ points apart as in a conventional repulsive-force method. The softening parameter is      │
│                          │ gradually sharpened, transitioning from broad global redistribution to local contact      │
│                          │ refinement. Candidate configurations are continuously centered and scale-normalized,      │
│                          │ while the best exact minimum/maximum distance ratio encountered is retained.              │
