│ patch_description        │ Replace the unstructured Gaussian sample with a reproducible multi-start optimization for │
│                          │ the actual scale-invariant squared distance ratio.  The solver keeps every candidate      │
│                          │ centered and normalized, then uses a continuation of smooth minimum/maximum               │
│                          │ squared-distance objectives.  The smooth minimum repels the current closest pairs while   │
│                          │ the smooth maximum contracts the current farthest pairs.  Several fixed-seed starts are   │
│                          │ evaluated and the candidate with the best exact (non-smoothed) minimum-squared-distance   │
│                          │ divided by maximum-squared-distance is returned.                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This directly targets the evaluator's metric while avoiding any dependency beyond NumPy.  │
│                          │ The returned array is always finite and has shape `(14, 3)`.                              │
