│ patch_name               │ multistart_spherical_refinement                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the fixed cuboctahedron-plus-axis construction, whose added axial points create   │
│                          │ short mixed distances, with a reproducible multi-start optimization on the unit sphere.   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The objective is scale invariant, so constraining candidates to the unit sphere removes   │
│                          │ irrelevant degrees of freedom. The optimization uses a smooth log-sum-exp approximation   │
│                          │ to the evaluator's true squared-distance ratio: it increases short pair distances while   │
│                          │ decreasing long pair distances. Several annealed sharpness stages progressively approach  │
│                          │ the nonsmooth minimum/maximum objective. Deterministic cube/axis, Fibonacci, and seeded   │
│                          │ random starts avoid dependence on one symmetry class and retain the best exact            │
│                          │ evaluator-style ratio encountered.                                                        │
