│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ deterministic_14point_optimizer                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ This implementation replaces random Gaussian points with a deterministic constrained      │
│                          │ maximin optimization.                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ It directly optimizes 14 three-dimensional points under the normalization that every      │
│                          │ pairwise distance is at most one, while maximizing the minimum squared pairwise distance. │
│                          │ Since the evaluator uses the squared minimum-to-maximum distance ratio, this is           │
│                          │ equivalent to the desired objective after normalization.                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The optimizer starts from a structured cube-plus-axis configuration and several           │
│                          │ deterministic perturbations, uses analytic constraint Jacobians when SciPy is available,  │
│                          │ and retains the best feasible result. A normalized structured fallback is included if     │
│                          │ SciPy is unavailable or optimization fails. The returned array always has shape `(14,     │
│                          │ 3)`, finite values, and positive maximum pairwise distance.                               │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
