│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ antipodal_line_polish                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Add a dedicated optimizer for antipodal 14-point configurations.  Such a configuration is │
│                          │ determined by seven unit vectors representing unoriented lines, with the returned points  │
│                          │ being each vector and its negative.  Its diameter is exactly 2, while its minimum         │
│                          │ distance is controlled by the largest absolute inner product between distinct line        │
│                          │ representatives.  This reduces the relevant search from 14 general points to the          │
│                          │ well-studied seven-line packing problem in R^3.                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The added deterministic multi-start projected optimization minimizes a progressively      │
│                          │ sharpened soft maximum of squared pairwise line correlations.  It includes the existing   │
│                          │ cube-plus-axis line arrangement as a structured start, together with fixed-seed random    │
│                          │ starts.  Every resulting candidate is still evaluated with the original exact ratio       │
│                          │ function before replacing the general optimizer's best result.                            │
