│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ seven_line_packing                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the cube--octahedron compound by a deterministic numerical construction of seven  │
│                          │ optimally spread unoriented lines in three-dimensional space, returning both antipodal    │
│                          │ endpoints of each line.                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ For antipodal pairs on the unit sphere, the diameter is exactly 2.  If the largest        │
│                          │ absolute inner product between distinct line directions is `c`, the minimum squared       │
│                          │ distance among all 14 endpoints is `2 - 2c`, hence the squared min/max ratio is           │
│                          │ `(1-c)/2`.  Thus minimizing the maximum absolute line correlation directly optimizes the  │
│                          │ evaluator objective for this centrally symmetric 14-point family.                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The replacement uses fixed-seed multi-start projected gradient descent on a smooth        │
│                          │ log-sum-exp approximation to maximum absolute correlation.  It uses only NumPy, maintains │
│                          │ unit directions after every update, retains the best actual maximum-correlation candidate │
│                          │ rather than merely the smooth surrogate optimum, and finally returns the seven directions │
│                          │ together with their negatives.                                                            │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
