│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ active_diameter_packing                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ This version removes the unnecessary constraint that every point must remain on the unit  │
│                          │ sphere. The problem is only invariant under global translation and scaling, so points are │
│                          │ instead centered and RMS-normalized after each update. This permits useful radial motion  │
│                          │ and possible interior-point configurations.                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ It uses a continuation objective based on smooth approximations to the logarithm of the   │
│                          │ minimum and maximum squared pair distances. Near the final continuation stages, it        │
│                          │ additionally constructs an active-contact force from pairs close to the current minimum   │
│                          │ and maximum distances. This directly expands limiting short pairs while contracting       │
│                          │ limiting diameter pairs. Multiple deterministic starts and small perturbations of strong  │
│                          │ symmetric seeds improve basin exploration while preserving reproducibility.               │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
