│ patch_name               │ active_contact_polish                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Add an exact-objective active-contact polishing phase after the smooth continuation. The  │
│                          │ smooth power objective is useful for entering a good basin, but at high powers it can     │
│                          │ still distribute force over pairs that are no longer limiting. The added phase explicitly │
│                          │ identifies pairs close to the current minimum and maximum distances, pushes the former    │
│                          │ apart and pulls the latter together, and uses a deterministic multi-step accept-only line │
│                          │ search evaluated with the true min/max ratio.                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This preserves the best point encountered rather than assuming the final smooth iterate   │
│                          │ is best. The tolerance schedule starts with a small contact band to coordinate nearly     │
│                          │ active constraints and ends with a sharp band focused on the actual bottlenecks.          │
