│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ projective_linepacking                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ This formulation uses the fact that an excellent 14-point diameter packing can be         │
│                          │ represented by seven antipodal pairs. The search is therefore performed directly on seven │
│                          │ unoriented lines in projective 3-space rather than on 14 unconstrained points. After      │
│                          │ fixing rotational gauge freedom, only 11 angular variables plus one coherence variable    │
│                          │ remain. SLSQP minimizes the largest squared inner product between lines; the returned     │
│                          │ antipodal configuration has diameter 2 and minimum squared distance \(2-2\max|\langle     │
│                          │ u_i,u_j\rangle|\). This is a much smaller constrained problem than optimizing all 14      │
│                          │ points and targets the relevant contact geometry directly.                                │
