│ patch_name               │ late_basin_hopping_polish                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Add a deterministic late-stage basin-hopping refinement around the best configuration     │
│                          │ already found by the broad continuation. The current search keeps only one best           │
│                          │ checkpoint and stops after its main annealing trajectory; this can leave an asymmetric    │
│                          │ contact graph close to, but not inside, a better local minimax basin.                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The added phase preserves the incumbent, creates several small reproducible asymmetric    │
│                          │ perturbations of it, and refines every clone using only sharp soft-min/soft-max           │
│                          │ objectives. This is inexpensive relative to the existing seven full trajectories,         │
│                          │ directly follows the exact squared-distance ratio objective, and retains every            │
│                          │ exact-ratio improvement rather than trusting the smoothed objective alone. The first      │
│                          │ narrow phase can alter the active contact graph while the second sharper phase settles    │
│                          │ the limiting minimum and diameter contacts.                                               │
