│ patch_name               │ persistent_contact_forces                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Replace purely instantaneous soft-min/soft-max force averaging with persistent,           │
│                          │ proximity-weighted contact coefficients. The exact objective is governed by a small       │
│                          │ contact graph, but smooth weights can be diluted by pairs that briefly enter a soft band  │
│                          │ while the configuration is moving. This change keeps exponential proximity weighting      │
│                          │ while maintaining an exponential-memory contact signal for near and far pairs. Persistent │
│                          │ limiting pairs therefore receive stronger force, particularly during the late             │
│                          │ narrow-temperature stages, while newly violated pairs still receive immediate weight      │
│                          │ through their proximity signal.                                                           │
