│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ adaptive_active_set_code                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ The current program uses six cube--axis initializations, Gaussian perturbations of scale  │
│                          │ 0.115, five soft-min/soft-max gradient phases with powers 4 through 64, and three         │
│                          │ accept-only active-contact polishing stages.                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This version changes the search configuration in several ways:                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - Uses seven axial-radius basins, including values closer to the cube circumradius        │
│                          │ regime.                                                                                   │
│                          │ - Uses a longer but more concentrated continuation schedule through powers 3, 6, 12, 24,  │
│                          │ 48, and 96.                                                                               │
│                          │ - Scales soft-min and soft-max weights relative to the current minimum and maximum        │
│                          │ distance, improving numerical conditioning at high powers.                                │
│                          │ - Uses momentum in the smooth phase to avoid repeatedly cancelling useful coordinated     │
│                          │ motion.                                                                                   │
│                          │ - Uses weighted active-set contact forces rather than uniform contact averaging: pairs    │
│                          │ closest to the current minimum and farthest from the current diameter receive greater     │
│                          │ force.                                                                                    │
│                          │ - Adds deterministic adaptive coordinate mutation search after the best continuous        │
│                          │ solution is found. Mutation scales shrink or expand according to acceptance rate, helping │
│                          │ resolve contact-switching barriers that gradient-only polishing can miss.                 │
│                          │ - Finishes with a tighter active-set pass while always retaining the best exact squared   │
│                          │ distance ratio.                                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The returned array remains deterministic, finite, and has shape `(14, 3)`.                │
