│ patch_name               │ diameter_constrained_polish                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Add a final simultaneous nonlinear-programming polish in diameter-normalized coordinates. │
│                          │ The coordinate perturbation phase can only improve one point at a time and is inefficient │
│                          │ once the optimum is determined by many coupled short- and long-distance contacts.         │
│                          │ Formulate the exact problem as maximizing a squared minimum distance `r`, subject to      │
│                          │ every squared pair distance lying in ``. Fixing one point removes translation, while the  │
│                          │ upper constraints normalize the diameter. SLSQP can then move all 14 points coherently    │
│                          │ and directly optimize the evaluator's squared-ratio objective. The result is retained     │
│                          │ only if its exact measured ratio improves the existing candidate, and the optional        │
│                          │ import/failure path preserves the current robust search result.                           │
