│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ persistent_contact_forces                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Replace uniform soft active-pair averaging in the annealing stage with persistent-contact │
│                          │ weighting. The nonsmooth diameter-packing objective is controlled by a small contact      │
│                          │ graph: pairs repeatedly near the current minimum distance should retain strong repulsion, │
│                          │ while pairs repeatedly near the diameter should retain strong attraction. Transient pairs │
│                          │ that only briefly enter a softmax tail otherwise dilute these forces.                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new update tracks exponentially averaged lower- and upper-band membership. It then    │
│                          │ reweights the existing differentiable log-distance forces by this persistence, while      │
│                          │ preserving a nonzero baseline so contacts can still change. The bands narrow as annealing │
│                          │ progresses, allowing broad early exploration and sharper late contact-graph polishing.    │
│                          │ This directly targets stable min/max constraints without changing the exact SLSQP         │
│                          │ formulation or return format.                                                             │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
