│ patch_description        │ This implementation uses the strong antipodal representation of a 14-point 3D code as     │
│                          │ seven unoriented unit lines, returning each optimized line together with its antipode. In │
│                          │ this representation the diameter is exactly positive and fixed at 2, while maximizing the │
│                          │ minimum point distance is equivalent to minimizing the largest absolute inner product     │
│                          │ between distinct lines.                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The search uses deterministic multi-start optimization of increasingly sharp power        │
│                          │ objectives, followed by accept-only active-contact polishing directly on the exact        │
│                          │ maximum correlation. This concentrates refinement on the pairs that currently determine   │
│                          │ the minimum distance, while preserving centering, spherical normalization, and antipodal  │
│                          │ diameter constraints exactly. The returned array has shape `(14, 3)` and is finite and    │
