│ patch_description        │ Preserve strong intermediate contact graphs from the broad continuation and branch late   │
│                          │ refinements from them, rather than refining only the single globally best exact           │
│                          │ checkpoint. Finite best-packing configurations can pass near several asymmetric basins    │
│                          │ during annealing; a configuration which is slightly inferior at 65%, 80%, or 92% can      │
│                          │ improve more under a sharp high-beta continuation than the final state of its original    │
│                          │ trajectory.                                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The edit records exact-score checkpoints, selects the strongest ones after the global     │
│                          │ phase, and performs paired deterministic/noisy refinements from each. The final added     │
│                          │ beta stage concentrates force on the true limiting pairs, improving local equalization of │
│                          │ minimum-distance and diameter contacts.                                                   │
