│ patch_name               │ survivor_reannealing                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Increase global basin coverage while holding the main continuation-force budget           │
│                          │ essentially constant: the two Fibonacci seeds differ only by a rigid rotation, so         │
│                          │ additional genuinely random starts are more valuable than very long trajectories from a   │
│                          │ few basins. Record each trajectory's own strongest exact checkpoint, rather than only the │
│                          │ globally best configuration. Then replace repeated perturbations of a single basin with   │
│                          │ survivor-based reannealing of the strongest independent basins. This better explores      │
│                          │ competing asymmetric contact graphs, while the final high-beta stages still provide       │
│                          │ accurate local refinement.                                                                │
