│ patch_name               │ contact_homotopy_pack                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ This version uses a contact-homotopy search rather than relying primarily on a fixed      │
│                          │ family of highly symmetric starts. It combines free-radial cube/axis seeds, perturbed     │
│                          │ antipodal seeds, twisted rings, and unrestricted random configurations. Each seed is      │
│                          │ evolved by a deterministic contact-force flow whose emphasis gradually shifts from broad  │
│                          │ pairwise separation toward the currently limiting minimum-distance and diameter contacts. │
│                          │ The best geometrically diverse candidates are then polished with the exact                │
│                          │ diameter-packing constrained formulation using analytic SLSQP derivatives.                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The main insight is that the best 14-point configuration is likely near, but not exactly  │
│                          │ inside, cube/octahedral or antipodal families. Therefore those structures are used only   │
│                          │ as broad basin generators, with independently perturbed radii and offsets before          │
│                          │ unrestricted optimization.                                                                │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
