│ patch_description        │ Add a second, contact-graph-aware polishing stage after each successful exact SLSQP       │
│                          │ solve. The first solve identifies the emergent minimum-distance and diameter contacts. A  │
│                          │ short regularized solve then reduces slack variation on those contacts while retaining    │
│                          │ every original feasibility constraint, followed by a final pure max-t solve. This can     │
│                          │ improve convergence in the degenerate active-set regime where many equivalent             │
│                          │ diameter/minimum constraints make a single linear-objective SLSQP pass terminate slightly │
│                          │ short of the best feasible packing.                                                       │
