│ patch_description        │ The current approach uses 7 seeds, a single 3600-step smooth continuation with beta       │
│                          │ increasing from 7 to 80, fixed direct gradient steps from 0.020 to 0.0025, and early      │
│                          │ random kicks. It does not preserve late-stage alternatives once a seed commits to a       │
│                          │ contact graph.                                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new implementation uses a broader structured seed family centered on cube--octahedron │
│                          │ configurations plus Fibonacci and random seeds. It replaces the single schedule with      │
│                          │ staged log-distance continuation using sharper beta values (5 to 190), normalized         │
│                          │ momentum directions, and checkpoint collection after intermediate and late stages. The    │
│                          │ strongest checkpoints are branched with small unrestricted-coordinate perturbations, then │
│                          │ refined with a high-beta continuation. Finally, exact active-contact polishing and        │
│                          │ adaptive accept-only coordinate search optimize the actual squared min/max ratio rather   │
│                          │ than only its smooth surrogate.                                                           │
